A||||3||SCCA FIERO||making an 88 coupe 4 cylinder auto tranny in to a manual V6
Z||000000||SCCA FIERO||05-13-99||08:07 PM||||  I have an 86 SE V6 with the 4 speed manual. The car got hit and was not fixed right. Then not too long after that i got hit again :( I can get an 88 coupe for a good price and i thought of making a great car from the 2. If anyone knows anyone that has done it let me know. I have several questions about it. I am wondering how the computer and wiring will go and things like that. Also the clutch has me worried to. The 4 speed in my 86 is pretty hard to shift and i was considering on maybe a 5 speed from a GT. I'm sure this can be done and any info would be nice.
Z||000001||theogre||05-13-99||08:18 PM||||If i understand right,,,,, the cradles are diferant, so that could be one problem.<p>you'll need the entire wiring, and ECM from the V6. very time consuming.<p>you'll need to move shifters, clutch parts, pedles, etc if the 88 is an auto. also very time consuming
Z||000002||PaUL||05-13-99||08:32 PM||||Well it looks to me like you can go 2 ways with the rear, use the 88 cradle and rear suspension or use the older one from the 86.<br>If you use the older cradle, less work is involved, you can just swap out the entire drivetrain. I believe both cradles bolt up to the frame the same way. Youd also have a very interesting fiero with the new front suspension and the old rear. <p>The entire ECM wiring harness can be removed from your 86. The ECM just unplugs from the harness and unbolts from behind the center storage bin. There is an opening in the bulkhead where the harness passes through. You can just unclip it and pass it out to the engine compartment.
Z||000003||SCCA FIERO||05-14-99||01:23 AM||||I guess getting my 4 speed to mate to the 88 cradle is the biggest problem. I would like a 5 speed but the reason i would do this is the cost would be less than buying an 88 equipped with a V6. My 4 speed is notchy and i'm sure a 5 speed would be expensive. Then again the 5 speed would solve a few problems with the cradle. What would a rebuilt 5 speed(for a V6 Fiero) go for?
